 tool-call syntax. Do not quote or place tool-call markup inside explanatory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 72 actions; a strong score needs about 39 or fewer. You are 1.8x over the target.\nIf you are not steadily making progress toward the level goal, commit to your single best hypothesis and the shortest sequence that tests it \u2014 do not exhaustively scan rows/columns or enumerate every option. Test one idea, read the result, then decide.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "SPACE had no effect (gameplay_changed=False). The bar is still at rows 12-15, cols 36-55. Let me try a different approach.\nMaybe the goal is to move the bar to overlap with the magenta (rows 4-7, cols 36-39). But the bar is 4x20, and the magenta is 4x4. If the bar is at rows 4-7, cols 36-55, it would overlap with the magenta at cols 36-39.\nBut earlier, when I tried to move the bar UP from rows 12-15, it was blocked. So the bar can't reach rows 4-7.\nWait, but earlier when the bar was at rows 40-43, it could move UP to rows 24-27. So maybe the bar can move UP from rows 40-43 to rows 24-27, and then from rows 24-27 to rows 20-23, and then from rows 20-23 to rows 16-19, and then from rows 16-19 to rows 12-15, and then from rows 12-15 to rows 8-11, and then from rows 8-11 to rows 4-7.\nBut I found that UP is blocked at rows 12-15 (can't move to rows 8-11) and at rows 24-27 (can't move to rows 20-23). So the bar can't move continuously UP.\nWait, but maybe the bar can move UP in a different column range. When the bar is at cols 36-55, UP is blocked at rows 12-15 and rows 24-27. But maybe if the bar is at a different column range, UP would work differently.\nActually, I think the key insight is that the bar